.TH RAM-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-19" "ram-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ram-revamped \- memory, swap and pressure in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ram-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ram-revamped
shows how much memory is in use in the tmux status line, with the memory
available, the swap in use, the memory pressure, a breakdown, the used and
total sizes, the commit ratio, the reclaimable size, the process that holds
the most memory, and a graph and a trend of the recent samples. macOS is
read from vm_stat and sysctl, Linux from /proc/meminfo and
/proc/pressure/memory.
.PP
The entry point
.B ram-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup key in one tmux call
and replaces the placeholders #{ram_percentage}, #{ram_icon},
#{ram_fg_color}, #{ram_bg_color}, #{ram_available}, #{ram_swap},
#{ram_swap_icon}, #{ram_swap_color}, #{ram_pressure},
#{ram_pressure_fg_color}, #{ram_breakdown}, #{ram_absolute}, #{ram_commit},
#{ram_reclaimable}, #{ram_top_process}, #{ram_graph}, #{ram_trend} and
#{ram_text} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored sample at once. When the sample is older
than the interval it starts one in the background, so the status line never
waits. The pressure and the top process are read only for a placeholder the
status line uses, at the detail interval. Run with no command on a terminal,
the tool offers a menu.
.PP
The pressure means different things on the two systems: on Linux it is the
ten second average of /proc/pressure/memory, the share of time some task
waited for memory, and on macOS it is the share of pages that are wired or
held by the compressor. The breakdown is wired, compressed, inactive and
free on macOS, and buffers, zero, cached and free on Linux. #{ram_commit} is
empty on macOS, which keeps no commit limit. #{ram_reclaimable} is cached,
buffers and reclaimable slab on Linux, and purgeable plus file-backed pages
on macOS.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the popup key and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored sample: percentage, icon, fg_color, bg_color, available, swap, swap_icon, swap_color, pressure, pressure_fg_color, breakdown, absolute, commit, reclaimable, top_process, graph, trend or text. The status line runs it, and it starts a sample in the background when the stored one is older than the interval.
.TP
.B refresh
Sample the memory now, read the pressure and the top process when the status line uses them, store the sample and say how much memory is in use.
.TP
.B card
Read everything now and print one row per figure: used, available, swap, pressure, used of total, the breakdown, the commit ratio, the reclaimable size, the top process, the history and the trend.
.TP
.B popup
Open a memory monitor in a tmux popup: btop, else htop, else vm_stat 1 on macOS, else free \-h \-s 1, else /proc/meminfo until Enter. The popup key runs it. On a tmux older than 3.2 the monitor opens in a window named ram.
.TP
.B daemon
Sample the memory and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per interval, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, each tool or file a figure comes from, the monitor the popup opens, the key it found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-top\-process\-label .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the popup key and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI RAM_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR RAM_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B RAM_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B RAM_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B RAM_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B RAM_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the monitor popup. off binds nothing. The default is M\-r, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_popup_width
The width of the popup, as tmux reads it. The default is 80%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_popup_height
The height of the popup. The default is 60%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_interval
Seconds a sample stays fresh before the memory is read again. The default is 5.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_detail_interval
Seconds the pressure and the top process stay fresh. The default is 60.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_render
jobs turns each placeholder into a call the status line runs. options turns it into a read of a tmux option that the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. Any other value means jobs. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_history_size
Samples kept for #{ram_graph} and #{ram_trend}. Zero means the default. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_medium_thresh
Percent at which the tier becomes medium. The default is 50.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_high_thresh
Percent at which the tier becomes high. The default is 85.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_warn_thresh
Percent of swap in use at which #{ram_swap_icon} and #{ram_swap_color} print. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_threshold
Percentage points between the oldest and the newest sample that move #{ram_trend} off steady. The default is 3.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_low_icon
What #{ram_icon} prints in the low tier. The default is one bar of three.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_medium_icon
What #{ram_icon} prints in the medium tier. The default is two bars of three.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_high_icon
What #{ram_icon} prints in the high tier. The default is three bars.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_low_fg_color
The style #{ram_fg_color} and #{ram_pressure_fg_color} print in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_medium_fg_color
The style they print in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_high_fg_color
The style they print in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_low_bg_color
The style #{ram_bg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_medium_bg_color
The style #{ram_bg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_high_bg_color
The style #{ram_bg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_active_icon
What #{ram_swap_icon} prints during the swap warning. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_active_color
What #{ram_swap_color} prints during the swap warning. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_up
What #{ram_trend} prints while the memory in use rises. The default is an up arrow.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_down
What it prints while the memory in use falls. The default is a down arrow.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_flat
What it prints while the memory in use is steady. The default is a right arrow.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_percentage_format
printf format of #{ram_percentage}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_available_format
printf format of #{ram_available}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_format
printf format of #{ram_swap}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_pressure_format
printf format of #{ram_pressure}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_breakdown_format
printf format of the four sizes of #{ram_breakdown}, in gigabytes. The default is W %sG C %sG I %sG F %sG.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_absolute_format
printf format of #{ram_absolute}: the memory in use, then the total. The default is %s / %s.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_commit_format
printf format of #{ram_commit}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_reclaimable_format
printf format of #{ram_reclaimable}. The default is %s.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_top_process_format
printf format of #{ram_top_process}: the name, then its size. The default is %s %s.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_icons
ascii labels nothing. nerd puts a Nerd Font glyph before every metric that takes a label. The default is ascii.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_fixed_width
on pads the used, available and swap percents on the left to four characters, so a change from 9% to 42% does not shift the status line. The default is off.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_percentage_label
Text printed before the used percent, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_available_label
Text printed before the available percent, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_label
Text printed before the swap percent, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_pressure_label
Text printed before the pressure, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_breakdown_label
Text printed before the breakdown, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_absolute_label
Text printed before used of total, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_commit_label
Text printed before the commit ratio, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_reclaimable_label
Text printed before the reclaimable size, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_top_process_label
Text printed before the top process, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_graph_label
Text printed before the graph, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_label
Text printed before the trend, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_percentage_width
Characters the used percent is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_available_width
Characters the available percent is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_swap_width
Characters the swap percent is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_pressure_width
Characters the pressure is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_breakdown_width
Characters the breakdown is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_absolute_width
Characters used of total is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_commit_width
Characters the commit ratio is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_reclaimable_width
Characters the reclaimable size is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_top_process_width
Characters the top process is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_graph_width
Characters the graph is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_trend_width
Characters the trend is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @ram_revamped_enable_logging
1 writes a sample that found no figures to ~/.tmux/ram\-revamped\-logs/ram\-revamped.log. It is read as a tmux option only. The default is unset.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored sample lives in
.BR @ram_revamped_percent ,
.BR _available ,
.BR _swap ,
.BR _pressure ,
.BR _breakdown ,
.BR _absolute ,
.BR _commit ,
.BR _reclaimable ,
.BR _top_process
and
.BR _history ,
with the time of the sample, of the pressure and of the top process in
options that end in _ts. apply records the placeholders the status line uses
in
.BR @ram_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @ram_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @ram_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.tmux/ram\-revamped\-logs/ram\-revamped.log
Samples that found no figures, written only while @ram_revamped_enable_logging is 1.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR vm_stat (1),
.BR proc (5),
.BR gum (1)
